.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-offbox-rotate 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-offbox\-rotate \- Rotate the state repository\*(Aqs finished sessions into its archive and remove their branches, discarding nothing
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten offbox rotate\fR [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-quiet\-runs\fR] [\fB\-\-print\-workflow\fR] [\fB\-\-install\-url\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rotate the state repository\*(Aqs finished sessions into its archive and remove their branches, discarding nothing
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<remote>\fR
The state repository\*(Aqs URL, whose finished sessions are rotated into its archive
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\-runs\fR \fI<quiet_runs>\fR
How many consecutive passes a session\*(Aqs branch must go unchanged before it is rotated (default 6)
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-workflow\fR
Print the workflow file that runs a pass on a schedule, and do nothing else
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-url\fR \fI<install_url>\fR
The install script\*(Aqs URL, which the printed workflow downloads and runs for this version
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
